  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting cultural heritage in peace time and in the event of armed conflict</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The workplan aims to support the development of policies, mechanisms and other measures to protect cultural property in times of peace and in the event of armed conflict, including through the ratification and implementation of the 1954 Hague Convention and its two Protocols. 

In the framework of the execution of the workplan, organization of four statutory meetings, capacity building activities for military and cultural heritage professionals, as well as implementation of targeted advocacy activities raising the number of States Parties to the 1954 Hague Convention and its two Protocols are foreseen. In addition, the workplan foresees to reinforce the capacity of the Secretariat to provide technical support to Member States in all aspects of the above-mentioned treaties.

The workplan will pay particular attention to the events to be dedicated  to the 70th anniversary of the adoption of the 1954 Hague Convention.</narrative>
  </description>
